# gRPC C++ Development

## Overview

gRPC is a high-performance RPC framework using Protocol Buffers for service definition and serialization. The C++ API supports sync and async patterns with 4 RPC types.

| Concept | Key Class / Tool |
|---|---|
| Service definition | `.proto` file |
| Code generation | `protoc` + `grpc_cpp_plugin` |
| Sync server | `ServerBuilder`, `Service` interface |
| Sync client | `CreateChannel()`, `NewStub()` |
| Async operations | `CompletionQueue`, `AsyncService` |
| Serialization | Protobuf messages |

## Prerequisites & Installation

### System Dependencies

```bash
# Required build tools
apt-get install -y build-essential autoconf libtool pkg-config cmake

# cmake 3.16+
cmake --version
```

### Build and Install gRPC from Source

```bash
export MY_INSTALL_DIR=$HOME/.local
mkdir -p $MY_INSTALL_DIR
export PATH="$MY_INSTALL_DIR/bin:$PATH"

# Clone (uses v1.78.1 as example; adjust to latest)
git clone --recurse-submodules -b v1.78.1 --depth 1 --shallow-submodules \
    https://github.com/grpc/grpc

cd grpc
mkdir -p cmake/build && cd cmake/build

cmake -DgRPC_INSTALL=ON \
      -DgRPC_BUILD_TESTS=OFF \
      -DCMAKE_CXX_STANDARD=17 \
      -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=$MY_INSTALL_DIR \
      ../..

make -j $(nproc)
make install
```

Note: Always install locally with `CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX` — there is no easy way to uninstall globally.

Verify:
```bash
protoc --version          # libprotoc 27.x+
which grpc_cpp_plugin     # $MY_INSTALL_DIR/bin/grpc_cpp_plugin
```

## Recipe 1: Define a Service (.proto File)

Proto3 syntax:

```protobuf
syntax = "proto3";

package routeguide;

// Simple message
message Point {
  int32 latitude = 1;
  int32 longitude = 2;
}

message Feature {
  string name = 1;
  Point location = 2;
}

// Rectangle for server-streaming
message Rectangle {
  Point lo = 1;
  Point hi = 2;
}

// Service definition with all 4 RPC types
service RouteGuide {
  // Unary RPC
  rpc GetFeature(Point) returns (Feature) {}

  // Server-side streaming RPC
  rpc ListFeatures(Rectangle) returns (stream Feature) {}

  // Client-side streaming RPC
  rpc RecordRoute(stream Point) returns (RouteSummary) {}

  // Bidirectional streaming RPC
  rpc RouteChat(stream RouteNote) returns (stream RouteNote) {}
}
```

4 RPC types:
| Type | Proto syntax | Client sends | Server sends |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Unary** | `rpc Name(Req) returns (Resp)` | 1 message | 1 message |
| **Server streaming** | `rpc Name(Req) returns (stream Resp)` | 1 message | stream of messages |
| **Client streaming** | `rpc Name(stream Req) returns (Resp)` | stream of messages | 1 message |
| **Bidi streaming** | `rpc Name(stream Req) returns (stream Resp)` | stream of messages | stream of messages |

## Recipe 2: Code Generation

Generate from `.proto`:

```bash
protoc -I protos/ \
    --grpc_out=. \
    --plugin=protoc-gen-grpc=$(which grpc_cpp_plugin) \
    --cpp_out=. \
    protos/route_guide.proto
```

Generates 4 files:
| File | Contents |
|---|---|
| `route_guide.pb.h` | Message class declarations |
| `route_guide.pb.cc` | Message class implementation |
| `route_guide.grpc.pb.h` | Service/stub declarations |
| `route_guide.grpc.pb.cc` | Service/stub implementation |

### CMake Integration for Codegen

```cmake
# CMakeLists.txt
find_package(Protobuf REQUIRED)
find_package(gRPC CONFIG REQUIRED)

# Or use the FindgRPC module from the grpc repo
# set(gRPC_CPP_PLUGIN $ENV{MY_INSTALL_DIR}/bin/grpc_cpp_plugin)

# Proto file
get_filename_component(hw_proto "protos/helloworld.proto" ABSOLUTE)
get_filename_component(hw_proto_path "${hw_proto}" PATH)

# Generated sources
set(hw_proto_srcs "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/helloworld.pb.cc")
set(hw_proto_hdrs "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/helloworld.pb.h")
set(hw_grpc_srcs "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/helloworld.grpc.pb.cc")
set(hw_grpc_hdrs "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/helloworld.grpc.pb.h")

add_custom_command(
    OUTPUT ${hw_proto_srcs} ${hw_proto_hdrs} ${hw_grpc_srcs} ${hw_grpc_hdrs}
    COMMAND ${Protobuf_PROTOC_EXECUTABLE}
    ARGS --grpc_out "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}"
         --cpp_out "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}"
         -I "${hw_proto_path}"
         --plugin=protoc-gen-grpc="${gRPC_CPP_PLUGIN}"
         "${hw_proto}"
    DEPENDS "${hw_proto}"
)

# Link your target against:
# target_link_libraries(your_target
#     ${hw_proto_srcs} ${hw_grpc_srcs}
#     protobuf::libprotobuf gRPC::grpc++ gRPC::grpc++_reflection)
```

## Recipe 3: Synchronous Server

### Implementing Service Methods

```cpp
#include "route_guide.grpc.pb.h"

class RouteGuideImpl final : public RouteGuide::Service {
 public:
  // Unary RPC — simplest
  Status GetFeature(ServerContext* context, const Point* point,
                    Feature* feature) override {
    feature->set_name(GetFeatureName(*point, db_));
    feature->mutable_location()->CopyFrom(*point);
    return Status::OK;
  }

  // Server-side streaming — use ServerWriter<T>
  Status ListFeatures(ServerContext* context, const Rectangle* rect,
                      ServerWriter<Feature>* writer) override {
    for (const auto& f : db_) {
      if (InRect(f, *rect)) {
        writer->Write(f);
      }
    }
    return Status::OK;
  }

  // Client-side streaming — use ServerReader<T>
  Status RecordRoute(ServerContext* context,
                     ServerReader<Point>* reader,
                     RouteSummary* summary) override {
    Point point;
    int count = 0;
    while (reader->Read(&point)) {
      count++;
      // process each point from client
    }
    summary->set_point_count(count);
    return Status::OK;
  }

  // Bidirectional streaming — use ServerReaderWriter<TReq, TResp>
  Status RouteChat(ServerContext* context,
                   ServerReaderWriter<RouteNote, RouteNote>* stream) override {
    RouteNote note;
    while (stream->Read(&note)) {
      // Can Write() at any time — streams are independent
      for (const auto& n : notes_) {
        stream->Write(n);
      }
      notes_.push_back(note);
    }
    return Status::OK;
  }

 private:
  std::vector<Feature> db_;
  std::mutex mu_;  // Thread safety!
  std::vector<RouteNote> notes_;
};
```

### Starting the Server

```cpp
void RunServer() {
  std::string addr("0.0.0.0:50051");
  RouteGuideImpl service;

  ServerBuilder builder;
  builder.AddListeningPort(addr, grpc::InsecureServerCredentials());
  builder.RegisterService(&service);

  std::unique_ptr<Server> server(builder.BuildAndStart());
  std::cout << "Server listening on " << addr << std::endl;
  server->Wait();  // blocks until Shutdown()
}
```

## Recipe 4: Synchronous Client

### Creating Channel and Stub

```cpp
class RouteGuideClient {
 public:
  RouteGuideClient(std::shared_ptr<Channel> channel)
      : stub_(RouteGuide::NewStub(channel)) {}

 private:
  std::unique_ptr<RouteGuide::Stub> stub_;
};

// Usage:
auto channel = grpc::CreateChannel(
    "localhost:50051", grpc::InsecureChannelCredentials());
RouteGuideClient client(channel);
```

### Calling RPC Methods

```cpp
// Unary RPC
bool GetOneFeature(const Point& point, Feature* feature) {
  ClientContext context;
  Status status = stub_->GetFeature(&context, point, feature);
  return status.ok();
}

// Server-side streaming — use ClientReader<T>
void ListFeatures(const Rectangle& rect) {
  ClientContext context;
  std::unique_ptr<ClientReader<Feature>> reader(
      stub_->ListFeatures(&context, rect));
  Feature feature;
  while (reader->Read(&feature)) {
    std::cout << "Found: " << feature.name() << std::endl;
  }
  Status status = reader->Finish();  // always call Finish()
}

// Client-side streaming — use ClientWriter<T>
void RecordRoute() {
  ClientContext context;
  RouteSummary stats;
  std::unique_ptr<ClientWriter<Point>> writer(
      stub_->RecordRoute(&context, &stats));

  for (const auto& point : points_) {
    if (!writer->Write(point)) break;  // broken stream
  }
  writer->WritesDone();  // signal end of writes
  Status status = writer->Finish();
  if (status.ok()) {
    // stats is now populated
  }
}

// Bidirectional streaming — use ClientReaderWriter<TReq, TResp>
void RouteChat() {
  ClientContext context;
  auto stream = stub_->RouteChat(&context);

  // Read and write in any order — streams are independent
  std::thread writer([&]() {
    for (const auto& note : notes_to_send) {
      stream->Write(note);
    }
    stream->WritesDone();
  });

  RouteNote server_note;
  while (stream->Read(&server_note)) {
    std::cout << "Got: " << server_note.message() << std::endl;
  }

  writer.join();
  Status status = stream->Finish();
}
```

## Recipe 5: Asynchronous API (CompletionQueue)

### Async Client

```cpp
void AsyncSayHello(const std::string& user) {
  CompletionQueue cq;
  ClientContext context;
  HelloRequest request;
  request.set_name(user);
  HelloReply reply;
  Status status;

  // 1. Initiate RPC and bind to CompletionQueue
  std::unique_ptr<ClientAsyncResponseReader<HelloReply>> rpc(
      stub_->AsyncSayHello(&context, request, &cq));

  // 2. Ask for the reply with a unique tag
  rpc->Finish(&reply, &status, (void*)1);

  // 3. Wait for completion
  void* got_tag;
  bool ok = false;
  cq.Next(&got_tag, &ok);   // blocks until tag arrives

  if (ok && got_tag == (void*)1) {
    // reply and status are ready
  }
}
```

### Async Server (CallData pattern)

```cpp
class CallData {
 public:
  CallData(Greeter::AsyncService* service, ServerCompletionQueue* cq)
      : service_(service), cq_(cq), responder_(&ctx_), status_(CREATE) {
    Proceed();
  }

  void Proceed() {
    if (status_ == CREATE) {
      status_ = PROCESS;
      service_->RequestSayHello(&ctx_, &request_, &responder_, cq_, cq_, this);
    } else if (status_ == PROCESS) {
      // Spawn new CallData to serve new clients concurrently
      new CallData(service_, cq_);

      // Process the request
      reply_.set_message("Hello " + request_.name());
      status_ = FINISH;
      responder_.Finish(reply_, Status::OK, this);
    } else {
      // FINISH: self-destruct
      delete this;
    }
  }

 private:
  Greeter::AsyncService* service_;
  ServerCompletionQueue* cq_;
  ServerContext ctx_;
  HelloRequest request_;
  HelloReply reply_;
  ServerAsyncResponseWriter<HelloReply> responder_;
  enum CallStatus { CREATE, PROCESS, FINISH };
  CallStatus status_;
};

// Server loop
void HandleRpcs() {
  Greeter::AsyncService service;
  ServerBuilder builder;
  builder.AddListeningPort("0.0.0.0:50051", InsecureServerCredentials());
  builder.RegisterService(&service);
  std::unique_ptr<ServerCompletionQueue> cq = builder.AddCompletionQueue();
  auto server = builder.BuildAndStart();

  new CallData(&service, cq.get());
  void* tag;
  bool ok;
  while (true) {
    cq->Next(&tag, &ok);
    static_cast<CallData*>(tag)->Proceed();
  }
}
```

## Recipe 6: SSL/TLS & Authentication

```cpp
// Server with SSL
grpc::SslServerCredentialsOptions ssl_opts;
ssl_opts.pem_root_certs = ReadFile("ca.crt");
ssl_opts.pem_key_cert_pairs.push_back(
    {ReadFile("server.key"), ReadFile("server.crt")});
auto creds = grpc::SslServerCredentials(ssl_opts);
builder.AddListeningPort("0.0.0.0:50051", creds);

// Client with SSL
auto creds = grpc::SslCredentials(
    grpc::SslCredentialsOptions{
        .pem_root_certs = ReadFile("ca.crt"),
        .pem_private_key = ReadFile("client.key"),
        .pem_cert_chain = ReadFile("client.crt")
    });
auto channel = grpc::CreateChannel("localhost:50051", creds);

// Token-based auth (metadata)
ClientContext context;
context.AddMetadata("authorization", "Bearer YOUR_TOKEN");
```

## Recipe 7: CMake Project Template

Full `CMakeLists.txt` for a gRPC project:

```cmake
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.16)
project(my_grpc_project)

set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED ON)

# Find gRPC
find_package(Protobuf CONFIG REQUIRED)
find_package(gRPC CONFIG REQUIRED)

set(PROTO_DIR "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/protos")
set(PROTO_FILE "${PROTO_DIR}/myservice.proto")

# Generate sources
get_filename_component(PROTO_PATH "${PROTO_FILE}" PATH)
set(PROTO_GEN_DIR "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/generated")

add_custom_command(
    OUTPUT
        "${PROTO_GEN_DIR}/myservice.pb.cc"
        "${PROTO_GEN_DIR}/myservice.pb.h"
        "${PROTO_GEN_DIR}/myservice.grpc.pb.cc"
        "${PROTO_GEN_DIR}/myservice.grpc.pb.h"
    COMMAND ${Protobuf_PROTOC_EXECUTABLE}
    ARGS
        --proto_path="${PROTO_PATH}"
        --cpp_out="${PROTO_GEN_DIR}"
        --grpc_out="${PROTO_GEN_DIR}"
        --plugin=protoc-gen-grpc="$<TARGET_FILE:gRPC::grpc_cpp_plugin>"
        "${PROTO_FILE}"
    DEPENDS "${PROTO_FILE}"
)

# Server
add_executable(my_server server.cc
    "${PROTO_GEN_DIR}/myservice.pb.cc"
    "${PROTO_GEN_DIR}/myservice.grpc.pb.cc")
target_include_directories(my_server PRIVATE "${PROTO_GEN_DIR}")
target_link_libraries(my_server
    protobuf::libprotobuf gRPC::grpc++ gRPC::grpc++_reflection)

# Client
add_executable(my_client client.cc
    "${PROTO_GEN_DIR}/myservice.pb.cc"
    "${PROTO_GEN_DIR}/myservice.grpc.pb.cc")
target_include_directories(my_client PRIVATE "${PROTO_GEN_DIR}")
target_link_libraries(my_client
    protobuf::libprotobuf gRPC::grpc++)
```

## Recipe 8: Health Checking

```cpp
#include <grpcpp/health_check_service_interface.h>

// Enable default health check service
grpc::EnableDefaultHealthCheckService(true);

// Server then responds to Health/Check RPCs automatically.
// Client can query:
#include <grpcpp/health_check_service_interface.h>
// health_check_service_interface.h provides the proto-generated client
```

13. **Manually linking (`-lgrpc++` only) fails with undefined symbols.** gRPC has dense transitive dependencies (absl, gpr, upb, re2, c-ares, ssl, crypto). Always use `pkg-config`:
   ```bash
   # WRONG — incomplete:
   g++ ... -lgrpc++

   # CORRECT — gets all transitive deps:
   g++ ... $(pkg-config --libs grpc++ protobuf)
   ```
   Without pkg-config, you'll hit errors like `undefined reference to gpr_log`, `undefined reference to absl::Mutex::Unlock()`, etc. Each one reveals another missing -l flag.

## Key Classes Reference

| Class | Role |
|---|---|
| `ServerBuilder` | Configure and build a server |
| `Server` | Running server instance |
| `ServerContext` | Per-RPC server-side context |
| `Service` (generated) | Interface to implement for sync servers |
| `AsyncService` (generated) | Interface for async servers |
| `ServerWriter<T>` | Write streamed responses |
| `ServerReader<T>` | Read streamed requests |
| `ServerReaderWriter<TReq, TResp>` | Read + write for bidi |
| `CreateChannel()` | Create a connection to server |
| `ChannelArguments` | Channel options (keepalive, load balancing) |
| `NewStub()` | Create client stub from channel |
| `ClientContext` | Per-RPC client-side context (deadlines, metadata) |
| `ClientReader<T>` | Read streamed server responses |
| `ClientWriter<T>` | Write streamed client requests |
| `ClientReaderWriter<TReq, TResp>` | Read + write for bidi |
| `CompletionQueue` | Async event loop |
| `Status` | RPC result (ok() or error_code + error_message) |

## Common Patterns

### Set Deadlines (always do this!)

```cpp
ClientContext context;
context.set_deadline(std::chrono::system_clock::now() + std::chrono::seconds(5));
```

### Error Handling

```cpp
Status status = stub_->GetFeature(&context, point, &feature);
if (!status.ok()) {
  std::cerr << "RPC failed: " << status.error_code()
            << ": " << status.error_message() << std::endl;
  // Common error codes:
  // DEADLINE_EXCEEDED, UNAVAILABLE, INTERNAL, PERMISSION_DENIED, etc.
}
```

### Keepalive

```cpp
ChannelArguments args;
args.SetInt(GRPC_ARG_KEEPALIVE_TIME_MS, 10000);         // 10s
args.SetInt(GRPC_ARG_KEEPALIVE_TIMEOUT_MS, 3000);       // 3s
args.SetInt(GRPC_ARG_KEEPALIVE_PERMIT_WITHOUT_CALLS, 1);
auto channel = grpc::CreateCustomChannel(
    "localhost:50051", InsecureChannelCredentials(), args);
```

### Custom Metadata

```cpp
// Client sends metadata
ClientContext context;
context.AddMetadata("custom-header", "value");

// Server reads metadata
std::string value;
auto md = context->client_metadata();
auto it = md.find("custom-header");
if (it != md.end()) {
  value = std::string(it->second.data(), it->second.size());
}
```

### Graceful Shutdown

```cpp
// Async shutdown pattern
server_->Shutdown();
// Wait for all outstanding RPCs to complete
// ...
cq_->Shutdown();  // Always shutdown CQ AFTER server!
```

## Pitfalls

1. **Thread safety in service implementations.** gRPC calls your service methods from multiple threads simultaneously. Use mutexes for shared state.

2. **Always call `Finish()` on client streams.** Not calling `Finish()` leaks resources. Pattern: `writer->WritesDone(); Status s = writer->Finish();`

3. **`ServerContext` is NOT reusable.** Each RPC gets a fresh context. Do not store and reuse across calls.

4. **`ClientContext` is NOT reusable.** Create a new one per call.

5. **CompletionQueue shutdown order matters.** Shut down the server first, then the CQ. Otherwise: undefined behavior.

6. **Unary RPCs are not truly one-call on the wire.** The framework still exchanges headers/trailers. Use streaming for true single-message patterns if needed.

7. **Don't install gRPC globally.** Use `CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX` to a local directory. There's no easy global uninstall.

8. **Missing `grpc_cpp_plugin`.** If protoc can't find it, use `which grpc_cpp_plugin` and pass the full path: `--plugin=protoc-gen-grpc=$(which grpc_cpp_plugin)`.

9. **Protobuf version mismatch.** gRPC and Protobuf must be from the same build. Always use the Protobuf bundled with gRPC, not a system-wide one.

10. **Forgetting `WritesDone()` on client streaming.** Without it, the server keeps waiting for more messages. Call `Write()` for all data, then `WritesDone()`, then `Finish()`.

11. **Bidi streaming: Write/Read on same thread causes deadlock.** In bidirectional streaming, calling `Write()` and `Read()` on the same `ClientReaderWriter` from the same thread can deadlock — `Write()` blocks when the internal buffer is full, but the server can only drain the buffer by reading, and the client can't read because it's stuck in `Write()`. Always separate writes and reads into different threads. Use a synchronization primitive (mutex + condition variable) to coordinate:

```cpp
// Shared state
struct WriteState {
    Request msg;
    bool has_msg = false;
    bool done = false;
    std::mutex mtx;
    std::condition_variable cv;
};

// Writer thread
std::thread writer([&]() {
    while (true) {
        Request req;
        {
            std::unique_lock lock(ws.mtx);
            ws.cv.wait(lock, [&]{ return ws.has_msg || ws.done; });
            if (ws.done) break;
            req = std::move(ws.hs);
            ws.has_msg = false;
        }
        if (!stream->Write(req)) break;
    }
    stream->WritesDone();
});

// Main thread reads
Response resp;
while (stream->Read(&resp)) {
    // process, then signal writer with next message
    { std::lock_guard lock(ws.mtx); ws.msg = next; ws.has_msg = true; }
    ws.cv.notify_one();
}
{ std::lock_guard lock(ws.mtx); ws.done = true; }
ws.cv.notify_one();
writer.join();
```

12. **Bidi stream handler may not be reusable.** After a client calls `Finish()`, the server's bidi stream handler thread may remain blocked in `stream->Read()` waiting for more messages. A subsequent client connection may fail with "Read failed" because the gRPC thread pool is exhausted or the handler state is stale. Always use `set_deadline()` on the client and restart the server process between bidi-stream test runs to ensure a clean state.

13. **Always set deadlines on ClientContext.** Without a deadline, a slow/stuck server handler can cause the client to hang indefinitely. Use `context.set_deadline(std::chrono::system_clock::now() + std::chrono::seconds(N))`. For long-running bidi streams, set a generous deadline (e.g. 900s) rather than omitting it.

11. **Bidi streaming same-thread Write/Read deadlock.** On the **client** side, calling `Write()` and `Read()` from the same thread is unsafe — if the server is slow to respond, `Write()` can block on backpressure while `Read()` never executes to drain responses, causing deadlock. **Always run `Write()` in a separate `std::thread`** and `Read()` in the main thread, using `std::mutex` + `std::condition_variable` to coordinate when requests are ready. Also always set `ClientContext::set_deadline()` (e.g., 300s for long inference) and enable keepalive on the channel via `ChannelArguments`. Pattern:

```cpp
// WRONG — same-thread Write/Read can deadlock:
while (!done) {
    stream->Write(req);    // may block on backpressure
    stream->Read(&resp);   // never reached → deadlock
}

// CORRECT — writer thread + main reader + condition-variable sync:
std::mutex mtx;
std::condition_variable cv;
HiddenStates pending;
bool has_pending = false, writer_done = false;

std::thread writer([&](){
    stream->Write(initial_req);
    while (true) {
        std::unique_lock lk(mtx);
        cv.wait(lk, [&]{ return has_pending || writer_done; });
        if (writer_done) break;
        stream->Write(pending);
        has_pending = false;
    }
    stream->WritesDone();
});

// Main thread reads responses and signals writer when new data is ready
stream->Read(&resp);   // non-blocking because writer is on another thread
// ... process, then signal next write:
{ std::lock_guard lk(mtx); pending = next_req; has_pending = true; }
cv.notify_one();

// Cleanup
{ std::lock_guard lk(mtx); writer_done = true; }
cv.notify_one();
writer.join();
stream->Finish();
```

## Verification Checklist

- [ ] gRPC installed: `ls $MY_INSTALL_DIR/lib/libgrpc++.a` exists
- [ ] protoc works: `protoc --version`
- [ ] Plugin found: `which grpc_cpp_plugin`
- [ ] Hello World builds and runs: build `examples/cpp/helloworld`
- [ ] Server starts and listens: `./greeter_server` prints "Server listening"
- [ ] Client connects and gets response: `./greeter_client` prints "Greeter received: Hello world"

